    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-3509",
      "problem": "The graph below shows the function $y=\\tan\\left(x+C\\right)$ for $-\\dfrac{\\pi}{2} < C < \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}.$ What is the value of $C?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14255079/assets/05d67f07067663e92125b524dc6f821c6848a29bf73729429de30bb50ff62ade.png)",
      "worked_solution": "Let's add the graph of $y=\\tan x$ to the plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14255079/assets/dc619961c3fd925670349b8e4b03f7103263184cb561b2605444f04403182d89.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\tan x.$\n\n- Then, shift it by $\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$ units **right**.\n\nTherefore, the given graph is $y = \\tan\\left(x-\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right)$ and hence the value of $C=-\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$.",
